While building a portfolio, one of the common challenges is dealing with Git and version control issues. Beginners often face difficulties in fetching the correct Git version, configuring Git on their system, or resolving authentication errors when connecting to GitHub. These problems can interrupt the workflow, cause confusion about repository states, and delay progress. Without proper troubleshooting, even simple tasks like cloning, committing, or pushing code can become frustrating, making it harder to maintain a smooth and professional portfolio development process.
